1
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:36,703
<i>Sorry, Agent Alex.</i>

2
00:00:36,786 --> 00:00:39,080
<i>We surprised you,</i>
<i>and it's not even your birthday yet.</i>

3
00:00:41,624 --> 00:00:42,584
<i>He trusted too much.</i>

4
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:44,502
<i>Trusting someone</i>
<i>is not that simple, Mikoy.</i>

5
00:00:44,586 --> 00:00:46,713
Do you still have doubts about Chiara?

6
00:00:46,796 --> 00:00:48,173
I trust you, Mikoy.

7
00:00:48,256 --> 00:00:49,507
But not Chiara.

8
00:00:50,049 --> 00:00:52,260
<i>She only has three island to search.</i>

9
00:00:52,343 --> 00:00:53,178
<i>What are we gonna do?</i>

10
00:00:53,261 --> 00:00:55,346
- Let's just sabotage her plan.
- How?

11
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:59,601
<i>I'll have them dig up</i>
<i>the whole island to waste their time.</i>

12
00:00:59,684 --> 00:01:01,227
Be careful with your plans, darling.

13
00:01:01,311 --> 00:01:03,855
What you might have to dig
is your own grave.

14
00:01:05,106 --> 00:01:08,151
<i>I heard that you're calling your dad.</i>

15
00:01:11,613 --> 00:01:13,573
I hope this battle ends soon,

16
00:01:13,656 --> 00:01:15,533
so you can visit your father.

17
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:18,411
Are you okay?

18
00:01:18,495 --> 00:01:19,704
Do you still have a fever?

19
00:01:19,788 --> 00:01:22,624
Your body was just overwhelmed
by yesterday's activities.

20
00:01:22,707 --> 00:01:23,958
Maybe you got infected

21
00:01:24,042 --> 00:01:26,085
because the woman
you helped was sick, right?

22
00:01:26,169 --> 00:01:29,005
Is it possible you got
infected by her, Angelito?

23
00:02:38,366 --> 00:02:41,494
- Right.
- There. I can actually see him.

24
00:02:46,124 --> 00:02:46,958
Excuse me for a bit.

25
00:02:49,460 --> 00:02:52,422
Hey! Aren't you taking a little too much?

26
00:02:53,464 --> 00:02:54,924
Do we even know you?

27
00:02:55,008 --> 00:02:57,594
It's just a little. Don't be so stingy.

28
00:02:57,677 --> 00:02:58,803
Wow!

29
00:02:58,887 --> 00:03:01,264
Maybe you're not even on the guest list.

30
00:03:01,347 --> 00:03:02,265
Who are you, anyway?

31
00:03:03,641 --> 00:03:05,059
You're a thief, aren't you?

32
00:03:05,143 --> 00:03:06,519
Me? Of course not!

33
00:03:06,603 --> 00:03:07,520
Come on.

34
00:03:07,604 --> 00:03:11,024
I only took some rice cakes,
spring rolls, and barbecue.

35
00:03:11,107 --> 00:03:12,317
A thief? Seriously?

36
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:14,861
I eat steak every day!

37
00:03:14,944 --> 00:03:16,946
Is that so? Hand it over.

38
00:03:17,030 --> 00:03:17,864
- Wait a second.
- Give it--

39
00:03:17,947 --> 00:03:18,781
- I'm kidding, I'm kidding.
- Give it to--

40
00:03:18,865 --> 00:03:20,158
- Hold on, hold on.
- Give it to me.

41
00:03:20,241 --> 00:03:22,285
- Wait a minute…
- Give it to me!

42
00:03:22,368 --> 00:03:24,495
Good grief. Go eat your steak!

43
00:03:26,956 --> 00:03:28,082
Such a bad attitude!

44
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:29,542
War freak!

45
00:03:37,550 --> 00:03:40,929
SIR, THEY GOT THE EVIDENCE
WE WEREN'T ABLE TO DESTROY IT

46
00:03:41,012 --> 00:03:42,889
Son of a skewer!

47
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:45,725
Time for Plan B.

48
00:04:11,668 --> 00:04:13,211
So he can be investigated.

49
00:04:20,468 --> 00:04:23,805
All of his transactions
with the Sinigang Cartel are in there.

50
00:04:23,888 --> 00:04:26,766
Your suspicions about
the corrupt senator were right.

51
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:29,143
But what I don't understand
about your story

52
00:04:30,186 --> 00:04:34,315
is that you told me he was determined
to capture the Moravianos,

53
00:04:35,275 --> 00:04:36,567
but why?

54
00:04:36,651 --> 00:04:38,361
The Sinigang Cartel is gone.

55
00:04:39,112 --> 00:04:40,530
Maybe he wants revenge.

56
00:04:40,613 --> 00:04:44,617
Or maybe he wants
to revive the organization.

57
00:04:44,701 --> 00:04:46,869
<i>But that's not what I'm thinking.</i>

58
00:04:47,495 --> 00:04:50,290
We have a much bigger problem now.

59
00:04:51,332 --> 00:04:53,793
Quintin knows about the bomb.

60
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:57,547
<i>He could already be working</i>
<i>with our enemies by now.</i>

61
00:04:57,630 --> 00:04:59,382
To help them find it.

62
00:04:59,966 --> 00:05:01,259
That's not impossible.

63
00:05:24,115 --> 00:05:25,950
Where are you, Mario?

64
00:05:39,088 --> 00:05:40,006
Nothing.

65
00:05:41,132 --> 00:05:42,300
No one came out.

66
00:05:44,677 --> 00:05:46,888
Come here. Have a seat.

67
00:05:48,556 --> 00:05:51,517
Guys, why don't we just
reschedule the documentary

68
00:05:51,601 --> 00:05:53,936
about the fishing village?

69
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:56,981
It looks like Angelito's condition
is getting worse.

70
00:05:57,065 --> 00:05:58,858
No, Sofie.

71
00:05:59,484 --> 00:06:01,986
We'd only be wasting time.
We're already here.

72
00:06:02,653 --> 00:06:03,988
I'll just get some rest.

73
00:06:04,072 --> 00:06:06,616
Then you guys can head there first.

74
00:06:06,699 --> 00:06:08,409
Go ahead and do it tomorrow.

75
00:06:08,493 --> 00:06:10,870
I'll follow as soon as I'm feeling better.

76
00:06:11,454 --> 00:06:14,707
But I think you need to go to a hospital,
or at least a clinic.

77
00:06:14,791 --> 00:06:16,709
You've been throwing up nonstop.

78
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:18,461
You might end up vomiting your intestines.

79
00:06:18,544 --> 00:06:22,048
There goes Ms. Overthinker again.

80
00:06:23,049 --> 00:06:24,342
That's nowhere near…

81
00:06:24,425 --> 00:06:25,343
Near what? Your intestines?

82
00:06:25,426 --> 00:06:27,261
It's actually pretty close to them.

83
00:06:27,845 --> 00:06:29,263
I meant your brain.

84
00:06:30,306 --> 00:06:31,349
Seriously.

85
00:06:31,432 --> 00:06:33,017
Oh, Angelito.

86
00:06:33,101 --> 00:06:35,353
You know, it's better
to have it checked early.

87
00:06:36,145 --> 00:06:37,105
Sofie.

88
00:06:37,730 --> 00:06:39,148
I'm really okay.

89
00:06:39,774 --> 00:06:42,443
You know, let's just think of this

90
00:06:42,985 --> 00:06:44,153
as something we're doing
for the community.

91
00:06:44,237 --> 00:06:46,906
This documentary is for them
once we finish it.

92
00:06:46,989 --> 00:06:48,491
Isn't that the whole point?

93
00:06:53,371 --> 00:06:54,914
It's your stomach, anyway.

94
00:07:02,505 --> 00:07:04,382
Where could Angelito be?

95
00:07:29,907 --> 00:07:32,285
Oh, my God, Angelito.
You're burning up with fever!

96
00:07:32,368 --> 00:07:34,912
Help! Help!

97
00:07:34,996 --> 00:07:36,456
Help!

98
00:07:40,543 --> 00:07:42,295
What's wrong? What's happening?

99
00:07:42,378 --> 00:07:44,338
Angelito has a very high fever.

100
00:07:46,466 --> 00:07:48,009
A doctor just arrived.

101
00:07:48,092 --> 00:07:50,636
From the island that was raided.

102
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:51,721
I'll go get them.

103
00:07:51,804 --> 00:07:53,014
Stay here for now.

104
00:07:53,097 --> 00:07:53,973
Okay. Thank you.

105
00:07:54,056 --> 00:07:55,641
- Wait for us.
- Okay.

106
00:07:57,602 --> 00:07:58,728
Sofie…

107
00:07:58,811 --> 00:08:00,771
Angelito, don't talk.

108
00:08:01,397 --> 00:08:02,940
What's happening to you?

109
00:08:17,914 --> 00:08:18,789
Mom!

110
00:08:18,873 --> 00:08:20,082
Mom, what are you doing?

111
00:08:26,881 --> 00:08:28,716
I'm sorry, Agent Alex.

112
00:08:28,799 --> 00:08:34,555
It's because… Mario told me
to use this to contact Angelito.

113
00:08:35,264 --> 00:08:36,724
I know it's against the rules.

114
00:08:36,807 --> 00:08:40,061
I'm sorry, but I just
couldn't stop worrying.

115
00:08:41,062 --> 00:08:43,064
The thing is, Mikoy,

116
00:08:43,147 --> 00:08:45,900
I can't reach Angelito.

117
00:08:47,026 --> 00:08:48,736
He's not replying to my texts either.

118
00:08:48,819 --> 00:08:50,696
Do you know when I last heard from him?

119
00:08:50,780 --> 00:08:51,906
It was a long time ago.

120
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:54,617
Take a deep breath.

121
00:08:55,618 --> 00:08:58,371
Are you feeling dizzy,
having trouble breathing?

122
00:08:59,622 --> 00:09:01,582
A little…

123
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:05,378
And I always feel so hot.

124
00:09:06,921 --> 00:09:09,340
<i>He's vomiting, feeling dizzy,</i>

125
00:09:10,550 --> 00:09:11,968
<i>and has erythema.</i>

126
00:09:12,051 --> 00:09:14,178
<i>He's been exposed to radiation.</i>

127
00:09:14,262 --> 00:09:15,471
You know, Mikoy,

128
00:09:15,555 --> 00:09:17,515
I think something bad
has happened to your brother.

129
00:09:17,598 --> 00:09:19,684
Mom! Don't say things like that!

130
00:09:19,767 --> 00:09:22,937
Maybe it's just…
Maybe there's just no signal over there.

131
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:25,189
Right?

132
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:27,316
All right, Aunt Tess.

133
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:30,444
To put your mind at ease,
I'll ask around at the agency.

134
00:09:30,528 --> 00:09:32,321
Please do. Thank you so much.

135
00:09:32,405 --> 00:09:36,367
I just can't stop worrying
until I get to talk to Angelito.

136
00:09:39,161 --> 00:09:40,580
Nothing.

137
00:09:43,249 --> 00:09:44,917
I'll just grab something outside.

138
00:10:04,729 --> 00:10:07,523
I saw your reaction earlier, and…

139
00:10:07,607 --> 00:10:11,110
it seems like my friend is suffering
from more than just a fever.

140
00:10:11,611 --> 00:10:13,529
What's really happening to him?

141
00:10:16,282 --> 00:10:17,533
I'm begging you.

142
00:10:18,159 --> 00:10:20,244
I have a lot of connections
in the government.

143
00:10:20,328 --> 00:10:22,872
My father is the Director General
of G.A.G.O.

144
00:10:22,955 --> 00:10:25,541
I can help Angelito.

145
00:10:26,083 --> 00:10:28,044
It's just that…

146
00:10:28,127 --> 00:10:31,505
I need to know what's
really happening to him.

147
00:10:37,136 --> 00:10:40,640
Have you ever heard
of the Broken Arrow incident?

148
00:10:41,807 --> 00:10:43,309
You mean the one where

149
00:10:43,392 --> 00:10:46,020
an American fighter jet carrying a bomb
crashed into the waters off Batanes?

150
00:10:46,103 --> 00:10:47,188
Is that the one?

151
00:10:50,566 --> 00:10:53,152
My fiancé, Enrico Santos, found it.

152
00:10:53,235 --> 00:10:56,238
But on the day we were supposed to meet,

153
00:11:00,493 --> 00:11:04,080
I've spent my entire life
searching for that bomb,

154
00:11:04,163 --> 00:11:05,998
and I believe

155
00:11:06,540 --> 00:11:08,542
it's here now.

156
00:11:09,794 --> 00:11:14,590
So do you think Angelito was exposed

157
00:11:15,591 --> 00:11:18,177
to radiation from that bomb?

158
00:11:51,085 --> 00:11:52,545
How's Aunt Tess?

159
00:11:53,754 --> 00:11:55,506
Mikoy's still trying to calm her down.

160
00:11:56,382 --> 00:11:57,675
Why aren't you with them?

161
00:11:59,677 --> 00:12:03,055
They don't need me
for every family matter.

162
00:12:05,015 --> 00:12:06,934
Besides, I wouldn't be much help.

163
00:12:10,771 --> 00:12:12,606
Still no word from him?

164
00:12:14,817 --> 00:12:18,529
By now, they should've already
infiltrated La Morte Bianca's hideout.

165
00:12:18,612 --> 00:12:21,240
But he hasn't even
sent a blank message yet.

166
00:12:21,907 --> 00:12:24,493
I actually had him monitored
when he left the country.

167
00:12:25,202 --> 00:12:26,412
Sianong said

168
00:12:26,495 --> 00:12:29,915
Cocoy already returned
to the Philippines with Los Bandidos.

169
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:40,384
What if…

170
00:12:41,343 --> 00:12:42,595
something happened?

171
00:12:53,314 --> 00:12:55,649
I still don't know
what was inside that package.

172
00:12:57,276 --> 00:12:58,861
We almost died because of it.

173
00:13:00,446 --> 00:13:01,405
What a shame.

174
00:13:01,489 --> 00:13:04,408
We didn't even get to read what it said.

175
00:13:04,492 --> 00:13:08,537
But thanks to you,
to your sacrifice, my darling,

176
00:13:09,371 --> 00:13:10,873
we get to live another day.

177
00:13:11,415 --> 00:13:12,708
Yes, even now,

178
00:13:12,791 --> 00:13:15,002
I can still feel that paper in my stomach.

179
00:13:16,504 --> 00:13:17,671
Actually…

180
00:13:19,173 --> 00:13:20,174
I managed to read something.

181
00:13:21,217 --> 00:13:22,218
It was just initials.

182
00:13:23,302 --> 00:13:24,470
"W.M."

183
00:13:24,553 --> 00:13:25,513
W.M.?

184
00:13:26,138 --> 00:13:27,139
Willy Monka?

185
00:13:27,973 --> 00:13:29,225
Wally Mayola?

186
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:30,851
Winnie the Moo.

187
00:13:34,688 --> 00:13:37,691
Was it from an ally or an enemy?

188
00:13:39,276 --> 00:13:41,779
An ally or an enemy?

189
00:13:41,862 --> 00:13:42,863
Exactly.

190
00:13:43,614 --> 00:13:44,949
I hope it's an ally.

191
00:13:45,824 --> 00:13:48,160
Because we need their help.

192
00:13:49,203 --> 00:13:50,621
Especially now.

193
00:13:51,330 --> 00:13:53,916
La Morte Bianca is starting to suspect us.

194
00:14:15,104 --> 00:14:16,397
Can I get through?

195
00:14:16,480 --> 00:14:18,899
This is important.
Someone's life is at stake.

196
00:14:18,983 --> 00:14:20,192
Please help me.

197
00:14:20,276 --> 00:14:21,318
Ouch.

198
00:14:23,737 --> 00:14:25,239
I hope there's a signal.

199
00:14:26,198 --> 00:14:28,367
Come on. Give me a signal.

200
00:14:31,954 --> 00:14:33,247
There! There it is!

201
00:14:34,123 --> 00:14:35,124
I have a signal.

202
00:14:37,334 --> 00:14:38,794
Hello, Daddy Sir?

203
00:14:44,842 --> 00:14:47,303
GLOBAL AGENCY FOR GOVERNMENT OPERATIONS

204
00:15:09,283 --> 00:15:10,451
Alex.

205
00:15:14,204 --> 00:15:15,623
<i>Sofie called.</i>

206
00:15:15,706 --> 00:15:17,207
<i>Angelito is sick.</i>

207
00:15:26,508 --> 00:15:27,885
Sir, what do you need us to do?

208
00:15:45,694 --> 00:15:47,237
<i>You stay at the safe house.</i>

209
00:15:47,321 --> 00:15:48,948
You need to protect the people there.

210
00:16:17,518 --> 00:16:20,145
UNKNOWN

211
00:16:51,677 --> 00:16:52,678
Alex, what's the update?

212
00:16:52,761 --> 00:16:55,180
Any news about Angelito?

213
00:16:56,724 --> 00:16:58,308
Mikoy, Angelito is sick.

214
00:17:08,610 --> 00:17:10,237
What's with that face?

215
00:17:11,572 --> 00:17:13,240
You look like someone died.

216
00:17:13,323 --> 00:17:14,575
I'm still alive.

217
00:17:15,617 --> 00:17:17,453
Don't tell me you're fine.

218
00:17:18,037 --> 00:17:20,873
Just look at yourself.
You look completely worn out.

219
00:17:20,956 --> 00:17:22,750
You're so stubborn.

220
00:17:24,376 --> 00:17:27,171
Now you know how I feel
whenever you're the stubborn one.

221
00:17:27,254 --> 00:17:28,130
You really are something.

222
00:17:28,213 --> 00:17:31,175
I'm already scared to death,
and you're still cracking jokes.

223
00:17:32,301 --> 00:17:33,802
Why are you scared?

224
00:17:33,886 --> 00:17:35,179
Do I look like a ghost?

225
00:17:37,598 --> 00:17:38,432
Wait.

226
00:17:38,515 --> 00:17:39,641
What did you say?

227
00:17:39,725 --> 00:17:42,144
What happened to Angelito?
He was poisoned?

228
00:17:42,227 --> 00:17:43,187
Mom, Mom.

229
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:45,731
Angelito was only exposed to radiation.

230
00:17:56,116 --> 00:17:58,243
I'll stay behind to secure the safe house.

231
00:18:00,454 --> 00:18:02,039
Oh, my poor son.

232
00:18:02,790 --> 00:18:04,333
Please don't worry.

233
00:18:04,416 --> 00:18:05,292
We'll take care of it.

234
00:18:17,387 --> 00:18:19,515
What if I lose you?

235
00:18:23,560 --> 00:18:25,145
Do you think I could handle that?

236
00:18:31,902 --> 00:18:33,862
There goes Ms. Overthinker again.

237
00:18:36,365 --> 00:18:38,575
But thanks for being an overthinker.

238
00:18:39,159 --> 00:18:40,494
Someone came to rescue me.

239
00:18:41,495 --> 00:18:42,704
It's not a rescue.

240
00:18:43,205 --> 00:18:44,998
It's called an extraction.

241
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:50,295
Whatever you call it, thank you anyway.

242
00:18:50,379 --> 00:18:52,798
My mind's all over the place.

243
00:18:52,881 --> 00:18:54,299
I can't even tell the difference anymore.

244
00:18:57,803 --> 00:18:59,179
Look at you.

245
00:18:59,263 --> 00:19:00,430
You've got wrinkles!

246
00:19:03,976 --> 00:19:05,102
Enough already.

247
00:19:13,360 --> 00:19:14,403
And besides,

248
00:19:14,486 --> 00:19:17,239
my treatment room
is already prepared, right?

249
00:19:27,875 --> 00:19:28,709
<i>Mom.</i>

250
00:19:29,334 --> 00:19:30,961
I'll take care of Angelito.

251
00:19:31,044 --> 00:19:33,213
I won't let anything
happen to him. I promise.

252
00:19:33,297 --> 00:19:35,549
I believe you, Mikoy.

253
00:19:36,383 --> 00:19:38,844
Bring Angelito home safely, okay?

254
00:19:38,927 --> 00:19:39,887
Please be careful.

255
00:19:39,970 --> 00:19:40,929
Yes, Mom.

256
00:19:41,013 --> 00:19:42,014
Yes, Mom.

257
00:20:03,035 --> 00:20:04,620
Should we go with her?

258
00:20:07,539 --> 00:20:08,540
Isabella.

259
00:20:33,565 --> 00:20:35,651
Money is my weakness.

260
00:22:00,569 --> 00:22:02,195
This is the island.

261
00:22:22,007 --> 00:22:25,677
White Eagle will drop you four clicks out
to avoid enemy detection.

262
00:22:31,975 --> 00:22:34,269
- Yes, sir.
- Agent Sianong is already there.

263
00:22:49,201 --> 00:22:51,078
There they are, Sianong!

264
00:22:51,161 --> 00:22:52,120
Awesome!

265
00:22:53,246 --> 00:22:55,332
Wow, there are so many of them!

266
00:22:55,415 --> 00:22:57,292
This agency is amazing!

267
00:22:58,919 --> 00:23:00,504
Over here! Over here!

268
00:23:00,587 --> 00:23:01,797
Here!

269
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:08,136
Who are they?

270
00:23:31,660 --> 00:23:33,578
<i>We will save your brother.</i>

271
00:23:42,003 --> 00:23:43,130
<i>Those are La Morte's men.</i>

272
00:23:43,213 --> 00:23:44,047
Sweetheart!

273
00:23:45,799 --> 00:23:47,092
Angelito, hurry.

274
00:23:50,846 --> 00:23:52,514
They shouldn't have that.

275
00:23:52,597 --> 00:23:53,515
Sofie.

276
00:23:55,058 --> 00:23:56,351
Angelito.

277
00:23:56,434 --> 00:23:58,353
- Mikoy!
- Mikoy, wait!

278
00:24:00,647 --> 00:24:02,941
Come on, Angelito. Let's go. Hurry up.

279
00:24:04,609 --> 00:24:05,610
Angelito.

280
00:24:07,696 --> 00:24:10,198
What? Did you find them?

281
00:24:10,282 --> 00:24:11,408
- They're not here.
- They disappeared.

282
00:24:23,628 --> 00:24:24,462
I don't have bullets left.

283
00:24:24,546 --> 00:24:25,797
Me too.
